Adapted from tools/rexglue-sdk/src/graphics/shared_memory.cpp in YesterMester/TheSimpsonsGameRecomp (commits 15feabc9
and 6c1695b3), which keeps the ReXGlue SDK's BSD 3-Clause License, see packaging/licenses/ReXGlue-LICENSE.txt.

Streams the vertex and index pages the game rewrites every frame. Every page the command processor uploads is made
valid and write-protected, so the guest's next write to it takes an access violation, a protection query and an
unprotect on the writing thread, and the next draw uploads the page and protects it again. A page whose writes faulted in
two frames in a row now becomes streamed: vertex fetch and DMA index requests upload it without making it valid or
protecting it, so it is uploaded again on every such request and never goes stale. Texture, resolve and memexport
requests still make it valid and protected. A streamed page uploaded more than 64 times in a frame is watched again, and
the set is learned again every 600 frames. With gpu_stream_skip_unchanged, a streamed request whose bytes still match
what the page was last uploaded with skips the upload. Only the D3D12 command processor calls OnGuestFrameEnd, so
nothing is streamed on other backends. Unlike the original, gpu_stream_dynamic_pages is off unless the title turns it
on, and the frame end only visits the blocks that faulted and the pages that were uploaded.

